From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:03:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: tty-sdio: return the TX credit when a push fails

mtty_write() and marlin_sdio_write() take a TX credit before pushing a
buffer and only the TX completion gives it back. A failed push, as
during a chip reset, kept the credit; after 63 failures every write
blocks for good.

Upstream: to be submitted to https://github.com/armbian/uwe5622
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/tty-sdio/tty.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/tty-sdio/tty.c b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/tty-sdio/tty.c
index 01ca0dd..0552e6e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/tty-sdio/tty.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/tty-sdio/tty.c
@@ -462,6 +462,7 @@ static int mtty_write(struct tty_struct *tty,
 		kfree(tx_head->buf);
 		tx_head->buf = NULL;
 		sprdwcn_bus_list_free(BT_TX_CHANNEL, tx_head, tx_tail, num);
+		up(&sem_id);
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
@@ -814,6 +815,7 @@ int marlin_sdio_write(const unsigned char *buf, int count)
 		kfree(tx_head->buf);
 		tx_head->buf = NULL;
 		sprdwcn_bus_list_free(BT_TX_CHANNEL, tx_head, tx_tail, num);
+		up(&sem_id);
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
